\sectiontitle{Project Abstract }

\vspace{0.05cm}

\instruction{

}

\vspace{0.12cm}

\answerbox{4.60cm}{
CareGrid is a centralized multi-hospital resource
coordination platform designed to help users find
suitable hospitals based on the availability of
beds, doctors, medical equipment, and other
facilities. Participating hospitals can maintain
their resource information in a shared system,
while the Central Health Hub processes requests
and retrieves matching information from the
database.

The project also focuses on preventing conflicts
when multiple requests are made for limited
resources, such as the last available ICU bed.

In the current phase, our work has focused on
the Python backend and relational MySQL database.
The user-facing interface and complete end-to-end
integration are planned for the next stage.
}

\vspace{0.70cm}

% ============================================================
% UPDATED PROJECT APPROACH
% ============================================================

\sectiontitle{
Updated Project Approach and Architecture 
}

\vspace{0.05cm}

\instruction{

}

\vspace{0.25cm}

\answerbox{6cm}{
The system follows a centralized architecture in
which hospital and resource records are stored in
MySQL and accessed through Python backend
request-processing modules.


The backend processes user requests, checks
hospital resource availability, and retrieves
information from MySQL through a CLI.

We have created relational tables to manage
hospital, doctor, resource, and appointment
records using SQL queries.

We plan to implement OS synchronization and
database transactions to prevent multiple
users from booking the same resource.

The next step is to develop the frontend and
connect it with the Python backend and MySQL
database using Flask.
}

